# TraPPE rigid CO2 (Harris & Yung, 1995 / RASPA3 reference).
# Type 1 = C_co2, Type 2 = O_co2.
# Energies in LAMMPS 'real' units (kcal/mol); lengths in Angstrom.
# eps_K converted to kcal/mol via k_B: 1 K = 0.0019872041 kcal/mol.
#
#   C_co2: eps = 29.933 K = 0.059490 kcal/mol,  sigma = 2.745 A,  q = +0.6512
#   O_co2: eps = 85.671 K = 0.170245 kcal/mol,  sigma = 3.017 A,  q = -0.3256
#
# Cross terms via Lorentz-Berthelot. LAMMPS uses arithmetic mixing with
# shifted LJ; tail correction off; PPPM Ewald for long-range Coulomb.
#
# Bond topology + intramolecular exclusions are handled by the wrapper:
#   * create_box_extra in the JSON adds bond/types and per-atom storage so
#     bonds can be declared.
#   * intra_bonds in the JSON tells the wrapper to issue the right
#     create_bonds single/bond commands after every (re)build, so insertion
#     and deletion moves keep the topology consistent.
#   * special_bonds (declared here) zeros out 1-2 (bonded C-O) and 1-3
#     (next-nearest O-O via the central C) LJ + Coulomb pair terms so the
#     huge intra repulsion at r << sigma drops out of the total energy.

# Masses (LAMMPSlib re-issues these later with the same values; no harm).
mass             1 12.011
mass             2 15.999

# Bond style + zero coefficient — the bond exists only as a topology marker,
# carrying no force.
bond_style       zero
bond_coeff       1 0.0

# Exclude 1-2 and 1-3 LJ + Coulomb (for any molecule with bonds declared).
special_bonds    lj 0.0 0.0 0.0 coul 0.0 0.0 0.0

# Pair style + Ewald + coefficients.
pair_style       lj/cut/coul/long 12.0
pair_modify      mix arithmetic shift yes tail no
pair_coeff       1 1 0.059490 2.745
pair_coeff       2 2 0.170245 3.017
set type 1 charge  0.6512
set type 2 charge -0.3256
kspace_style     pppm 1.0e-5
